** Load balancing of a distributed model: each process creates only the elements it computes, and the model
** is repartitioned with the element numbers as element costs (load-balance-costs=elementNumber) -- uneven and
** deterministic -- so that at the output increment 20, once the material has yielded, elements move between
** the processes (migration): the new process creates them and receives their state. A body force on every
** element makes each process create the loaded elements touching its own as well, before and after. The
** result, and the restart checkpoint written after the migration, are those of a serial run.
*modelGenerator, generator=planeRectQuad, name=gen
l=40
h=10
nX=16
nY=4
elType=CPE4

*material, name=VonMises, id=myMaterial
210000, 0.3, 550, 1000, 200, 1400, 1, 7.8e-9

*section, name=section1, material=myMaterial, type=plane, thickness=1
all

*job, name=rebalanceJob, domain=2d
*solver, solver=NEDMPI, name=theSolver
output-frequency=20
load-balance-costs=elementNumber

*fieldOutput
>>perNode, name=uRight, nSet=gen_right, field=displacement, result=U, f(x)='np.mean(x[:,0])', saveHistory=True
>>perElement, elSet=all, result=stress, name=S11, quadraturePoint=0, f(x)='x[:,0]'

*output, type=restart, name=restart
writeInterval=2, baseName=restart, numberOfFilesToKeep=1

*step, type=adaptiveForExplicitSimulations, solver=theSolver
maxInc=1, minInc=1e-12, maxNumInc=1000, maxIter=25, stepLength=0.4
>>dirichlet, name=left, nSet=gen_left, field=displacement, 1=0, 2=0
>>dirichlet, name=right, nSet=gen_right, field=displacement, 1=1.0
>>bodyForce, name=gravity, elSet=all, forceVector='0.0, -1e-2', f(t)=t
